meta {
  name: EnsureUser
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.IdentityService/EnsureUser
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "subject": "emulator-subject",
      "email": "dev@dop.local",
      "email_verified": true,
      "name": "Dev Local",
      "provider": "password",
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0013, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  Idempotent by design: it is called on EVERY first sign-in. Repeating it with the
  same `idempotency_key` returns the same user, with no duplicate (ADR-0013).

  The `subject` is the normalized principal's — not Firebase's raw `uid`.
}
